      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-09T00:44:15Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): carry the machined body into the next setup\n\nThe program sim no longer refuses a program that spans setups holding\nthe part differently. On entering such a setup (or one placed relative\nto the previous with #316's link), the body the earlier setups left is\ncarried through setup_relative::transform_between: a two-sided column\nbody (top and floor per column) re-indexed exactly onto the image\nlattice for flips over X/Y and quarter turns about Z - never\nre-sampled (#308). After a flip the floor is judged against the part's\nbottom, so a gouge cut before the flip is still a gouge after it.\nSame-held unlinked setups keep the M3.2 A clip. Turns the lattice\ncannot carry exactly, and lathe/mill-turn machines, refuse by name.\nstock_sim::incoming_body exposes a setup's incoming stock for #318 and\n#320.\n\nFixes #317\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
